module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Basic
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.FormallySmoothAdic

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

namespace RingHom

/-- Restrict adic formal smoothness along a residue-field isomorphism, with the
algebra structure explicitly induced by that map.
Source: Stacks Project, Remark 07NS, first paragraph (change of residue scalars).
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-residue-formally-smooth-transport)

Proof: The bijective residue map is a ring equivalence e : k₀ ≃ k. Give E the
k₀-action obtained by composing its k-action with e. For a square-zero lifting
problem over k₀, give the test ring a k-action by composing with e.symm. Then a
k₀-algebra map from E is a k-algebra map for these structures: write each element
of k as e(a) and use the original scalar compatibility. Apply the given k-adic
lifting property. Restrict the lift back along e; the quotient equality and the
vanishing of the prescribed ideal power are unchanged. If the test ring is in a
larger universe than the given lifting property allows, choose representatives of
all quotient images of E and take the k-subalgebra generated by these representatives.
Its cardinality is bounded by max(v,w). Its intersection with the square-zero ideal
is square-zero, and its quotient injects into the original quotient. Thus the map
from E factors through that quotient and retains its power bound. Shrink the
subalgebra to Type(max(v,w)), apply the given lifting property, and compose with
its inclusion into the test ring. If the allowed test universe is smaller, ULift
it before applying the original property and transport the lift back. This proves
the assertion for both orders of the universe levels, with exactly the constructed
action rather than an unspecified existential algebra structure. -/
theorem residue_formallySmooth_transport
    {A₀ : Type u} {A : Type v} {E : Type w}
    [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing E]
    [IsLocalRing A₀] [IsLocalRing A]
    [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) E]
    (n : Ideal E) (α : A₀ →+* A) [IsLocalHom α]
    (hres : Function.Bijective (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map α))
    (hfs : Algebra.FormallySmoothAdic (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) E n) :
    letI : Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A₀) E :=
      ((algebraMap (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A) E).comp
        (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map α)).toAlgebra
    Algebra.FormallySmoothAdic (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A₀) E n := by sorry

end RingHom
